From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Requirements: tilelang 0.1.16

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm@6d66eed35b0ab1cc0e05f00e83ef638ba10ae3db
with the 648-patch serving series unchanged.

Rationale: the image build's cross-consumer requirement check rejects
tilelang 0.1.16+snapshot.<tree> against `tilelang==0.1.15` — PEP 440 local
versions only satisfy `==` on the same base version. The tilelang-0116
candidate moves the pin to the 0.1.16 cut, so vLLM's declared floor moves
with it.

Quality: a requirements declaration only; no code, no import, no runtime
path changes. The installed wheel is still the patched snapshot whose
identity is the pre-metadata tree (0012 re-key).

Tests: the image build's own version assertion (requirements/cuda.txt vs
the built wheel) is the test; it failed before this patch and passes after.

Upstream status: local pin alignment; not submitted (the LIL branch pins
0.1.15 until its own refresh).
---
 requirements/cuda.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/requirements/cuda.txt b/requirements/cuda.txt
--- a/requirements/cuda.txt
+++ b/requirements/cuda.txt
@@ -20,4 +20,4 @@
 flashinfer-cubin==0.7.1
 apache-tvm-ffi==0.1.11
-tilelang==0.1.15
+tilelang==0.1.16
 nvidia-cudnn-frontend>=1.19.1
